// "Mill N" ([CR#701.17a]): the imperative YOU-form self-mill — you put the top
// N cards of your library into your graveyard, as one group — a single
// instruction, not per-card like draw ([CR#121.2]); clamped to library size
// ([CR#701.17b]). Scry's sibling on the
// mill lane: the keyword action as DATA — a `Composite` whose tag is
// `Mill(You, n)` and whose body is the batch `MoveGroup` of the top N of your
// library to your graveyard. The declarative-subject form ("Target player mills
// N cards.") is the `Mills(who, n)` macro; this is the bare you-imperative.
//
// Usage: Mill(3) -> "Mill three cards."
(
    name: "Mill",
    template: "mill ${0:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Count],
    body: Composite(
        Mill(You, Param(0)),
        MoveGroup(
            group: TopOfLibrary(count: Param(0)),
            arrangement: AnyOrder,
            to: Graveyard,
        ),
    ),
)
